  "details": "One of my old SDK2 worlds relied on a trigger which just happened to be at the world origin (0 0 0)\n\nFrom the past we've seen several times that when players initialize they temporarily appear at world origin.\n\nPreviously players would load just fine, but apparently at some point players started activating triggers mid-initialization which causes unexpected behavior.\n\nHere is an example world to demonstrate the behavior:\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_bd51fe80-8c4e-4180-bc5b-862fb8c9ea4e\n\nThis world has a road that leads to the end of the road, there is a wall in the middle that blocks the road but it is disabled by default..\n\nIf you step into a red trigger it will enable the wall, the trigger is located on the origin of the world. The spawn point is located outside the origin.\n\nExpected: You are not supposed to see a wall until you step into a trigger.\n\nResult: You see the wall before you stepped into a trigger.",
